{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": "Hooks in shell form: each `command` is one string, java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" <mode>, and no entry carries `args`. The GitHub Copilot CLI reads this same file, runs `command` alone and ignores `args`, so the exec form used before launched a bare `java` that exited 1 — and a preToolUse hook that exits neither 0 nor 2 denies the call there, so every Edit, Shell and Read was denied. Claude Code substitutes the quoted placeholder before its shell runs (sh -c, Git Bash on Windows, PowerShell without Git Bash); a Unix shell under Copilot expands the same text from the environment. One process per entry still: `schema` refuses a pipe, a chain, a redirect or a substitution in `command`, and holds every ArchHook entry to `settings.archhook_command_pattern`. A project path holding a double quote, `$` or a backtick would split the string — `doctor` warns on its `Hook path` line. Design: .claude/decisions/0168-hooks-in-shell-form.md. The `if` field filters by permission rule before spinning up the process: without it, every edit to any file would pay for a JVM startup. The `audit` entries record the execution trail of every skill and agent of this project into .claude/audit-usage/ — opened by a `/command` or by the model's own Skill/Agent call; plugin skills and runtime agents are not recorded. Each entry returns immediately when that directory does not exist or no run is open, so the JVM cost outside a run is a process start and nothing more. Delete the directory to switch the trail off. The `guard` entries keep each skill inside the territory its class declares in .claude/schemas/extensions.json (`skill_classes`), freeze the specs of approved use cases, and refuse a Skill call to a build-class skill while a design run is open. The Write|Edit entry carries no `if` on purpose: territory is deny-by-default, so a path filter would recreate the hole it closes — a design run once wrote a service block into docker-compose.yml, a file no forbidden-path list named. It returns immediately when no phase is open, which is every write outside a skill invocation. The `Bash` entry is the same check reached from the other side: every other enforcement here matches on a tool name, so a heredoc, a `sed -i` or a `tee` passed through all of them and wrote into a frozen UC-NNN folder with nothing objecting. It reads the command for the write shapes listed in `guard.bash_write_shapes` and checks the paths it can read literally; a target it cannot resolve is skipped in silence, which is what keeps a hook that runs on every shell command from blocking a build. The same entry refuses a shell read (`cat`, `wc`, `grep`, `<`, …) of a path in `guard.secret_paths` of .claude/schemas/extensions.json — the list the `Read(...)` lines of `permissions.deny` below are derived from, and `schema` fails when they drift. Under the GitHub Copilot CLI and VS Code, which read no `permissions` block from this file, .github/hooks/archhook.json runs `guard read` on their own file reads; Claude Code never reads that file. Design: .claude/decisions/0173-secret-read-guard-for-copilot.md. The write matchers are one list: `audit file`, `format` and `check` used to match `Write|Edit` alone, so a `MultiEdit` was territory-checked and then never boundary-checked, formatted, or recorded in the trail. On `Stop`, `guard sweep` is the backstop behind both write guards: it reads what changed on disk since the baseline `guard prompt` took, so it catches the shell spellings the parser cannot read, and it admits a spec's `status:` close and its checklist toggles by comparing against `git show HEAD:`. It is git-shaped — a path git ignores is never swept. `compose gate` is the same report `doctor` and the bare `compose` use, silent while healthy and exit 2 otherwise: the check existed, `docker-architect` step 7 called it not optional, and it had never been run, which is how a broker that no host client could reach shipped on day one. Permissions: the pipeline skills are pre-authorized so nobody approves them one by one mid-run — that is where broad rules like `Bash(git *)` slipped in. `git push` is always `ask`; never widen it to an allow. `enabledPlugins` turns off, in this project only, plugins a developer may have enabled at user level whose skills compete with this pipeline for automatic invocation; the list is `settings.blocked_plugins` in .claude/schemas/extensions.json, and `schema` fails when an entry is missing here. Re-enable one for yourself in the untracked .claude/settings.local.json. Design: .claude/decisions/0138-block-colliding-plugins-and-report-shadowed-skills.md. Every entry launches the precompiled `.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar` (`java -jar`), not the source: a source launch recompiled the whole file on every call, ~3.3 s against ~0.3 s. `schema` and `doctor` report a jar built from another version of `ArchHook.java`; `java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java build` rebuilds it under the pinned JDK. `format` and `check` carry `if: Edit(**/*.java)` — both return at their first line for anything else, so the filter loses nothing. Path rules in `if` are matched only through `Edit(...)`/`Read(...)`, and `Edit` covers every built-in tool that writes a file, `Write` included — which is why no `if` here spells `Write(...)`. Design: .claude/decisions/0075-precompiled-hook-jar.md. `SubagentStart` runs `context subagent`, which hands gof-design-patterns' catalog to every agent whose `agent_classes` entry declares `pattern_catalog: true`, before its first turn, and prints nothing for any other agent. No `matcher` on purpose: a regex naming agents is exactly what a future Java-writing agent would miss — the flag in extensions.json is the filter. It exists because `gof-design-patterns` is manual-only, and a skill with `disable-model-invocation: true` cannot be preloaded through an agent's `skills:` field. Design: .claude/decisions/0077-pattern-catalog-injected-at-subagent-start.md.",
  "hooks": {
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit prompt",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" guard prompt",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(.claude/**/*.md)",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" schema",
            "statusMessage": "Validating frontmatter...",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Skill|skill|Task|Agent",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit call",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" guard call",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "AskUserQuestion",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit ask",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" guard write",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" guard bash",
            "statusMessage": "Checking what this command writes...",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PermissionRequest": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit perm",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PermissionDenied": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit perm",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit fail",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" context subagent",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" tests agent-start",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit agent",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" tests agent-end",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit compact",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "StopFailure": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit stopfail",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit close",
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "AskUserQuestion",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit answer",
            "timeout": 20
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit file",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(**/*.java)",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" format",
            "statusMessage": "Formatting...",
            "timeout": 90
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(**/*.java)",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" check",
            "statusMessage": "Checking boundaries...",
            "timeout": 180
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(.claude/**/*.md)",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" schema",
            "statusMessage": "Validating frontmatter...",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" audit flush",
            "statusMessage": "Recording the execution trail...",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" schema",
            "statusMessage": "Validating frontmatter...",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" guard sweep",
            "statusMessage": "Sweeping what this turn wrote...",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" compose gate",
            "statusMessage": "Checking compose services...",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" tests",
            "statusMessage": "Running the verify gate on changed modules...",
            "timeout": 600
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(./mvnw:*)",
      "Bash(mvnw.cmd:*)",
      "Bash(./gradlew:*)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java doctor)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java schema)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java compose)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java compose gate)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java build --verify)",
      "Bash(java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java audit summary)",
      "Bash(git status:*)",
      "Bash(git diff:*)",
      "Bash(git log:*)",
      "Skill(new-feature)",
      "Skill(new-feature-implement)",
      "Skill(use-case-design)",
      "Skill(domain-modeling)",
      "Skill(rest-api-architect)",
      "Skill(persistence-architect)",
      "Skill(messaging-architect)",
      "Skill(test-architect)",
      "Skill(docker-architect)",
      "Skill(git-publish)"
    ],
    "ask": [
      "Bash(git push:*)",
      "Bash(gh repo create:*)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Read(./**/*.env)",
      "Read(./**/secrets/**)",
      "Read(./**/application-prod.yml)",
      "Read(./**/application-prod.yaml)",
      "Read(./**/*.pem)",
      "Read(./**/*.p12)",
      "Bash(git push --force:*)"
    ]
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "superpowers@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "mattpocock-skills@claude-plugins-official": false
  }
}
